KG42.register("clusters-3d9339aae33f5c343cca13f3",{"id":"09-local_flexibility::v142-d-CL003","paper":"09-local_flexibility","label":"Willingness-to-pay confidentiality and operator-role separation in request forwarding","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"Willingness-to-pay confidentiality and operator-role separation in request forwarding","market_meaning":"When forwarding DSO service requests to aggregators, the market operator does not disclose the DSO's willingness to pay; under the unbundling principle discussed in the literature, a DSO simultaneously serving as the market operator constitutes an incompatible role arrangement.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["coordination"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The confidentiality obligation concerns request forwarding in EcoGrid 2.0 auctions; the determination of role incompatibility is conditional on the principle of separating network operation from commercial activities discussed in the literature and is not extended into an unconditional legal conclusion for all jurisdictions.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"Request information is the input, the market operator bears the obligations to forward requests and preserve willingness-to-pay confidentiality, and the role-separation provision restricts the entity that may perform this function. This governance rule has independent market significance; the information-flow narrative does not automatically create new dependency edges to other chains.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Fully retains confidentiality in request forwarding and the conditional constraints on entity roles, without merging the DSO buyer, operator, and aggregator into the same entity."}],"connections":[],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G010","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The frozen graph contains only a coordination-function node and cannot separately reference the identities of the DSO buyer and aggregator; the related entity proposals still await review. Procedural governance obligations can be expressed, but the shared coordination node cannot establish that the DSO is the market operator.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E18"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-dso-request","v141-b-g01-prop-aggregator","v141-b-g02-prop-aggregator-participation"],"required_work":"Manually examine the boundaries between the entity proposals and the existing coordination node; if entity-level information interfaces are required, represent them explicitly in subsequent ontology and C versions, without inserting entity nodes or information-flow scientific edges in this round."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G011","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B evidence for the request-confidentiality and unbundling provisions remains unverified, and neither the scope of the literature's discussion nor the transcriptions have undergone an independent source-text audit; this cluster is a procedural candidate for manual examination.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the original text's scope regarding the information subject to confidentiality, the forwarding entity, and the unbundling conditions; retain the current evidence status and do not extend the literature's principle into an unsupported universal prohibition."}]},"rule_refs":["09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-5bf16b611081f62c"]});
